<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/1st-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Russo-Crimean Wars</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">16th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Russo-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimean-war">Crimean Wars</a> were a series of conflicts in the sixteenth century between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-duchy-of-moscow">Grand Duchy of Moscow</a>, later the Tsardom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, and the Crimean Khanate, often backed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>. Crimean <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tatars">Tatar</a> raids reached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> and burned it in 1571, but a Russian army under Mikhail Vorotynsky defeated the Crimean host at Molodi in 1572, ending the threat of Crimean conquest of Muscovy.</p></div>
